00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Become a Title22 partner — what a code does, what it pays, and where referrals come from.

00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:13.500
Three ways in: as a trainer, as an affiliate, or as a graduate already running a home. Nothing stops you being two of them.

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:22.500
A code is a longer trial. Someone arriving on your link gets 90 days instead of the default 14.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:31.500
One row per code: your link, how many signed up, how many are paying, and the rate on record.

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:42.500
You earn on a paid subscription, every month they stay. 20% is the default; rates are agreed per partner, and Eli pays directly.

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:53.500
Two traps: only signups are tracked, not clicks — and a code cannot attach to an account that already exists. Send your link before they sign up.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:04.500
The referrals that convert: your own graduates the week they are licensed, homes fresh from an inspection, and anyone hiring or opening a second home.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:12.500
The line that works: "use my link and you get 90 days free instead of 14." Specific, true, and free to check.

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:22.500
To start: email hello@title-22.com, confirm your rate, and get your code. If you teach, ask for a classroom account too — it is a separate request.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.500
Everything here is at title-22.com/partners. Email hello@title-22.com to get your code.
